From f4fcf7d9f0290ae037c47fe33201215b906c408d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 05:39:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Let the question abilities ask any question

Scout, Uncanny Eye and Tactician offered only the book's three questions
in a select (issue #63, decision 5). The sheet now has a "Question to ask"
box for any question, with the book's questions under the empty box as
examples a tap fills in. The cost is still spent and the log names the
question as written.

The server takes the question as free text in use_ability's question
field, cleaned to one line (runs of spaces and line breaks become one
space, characters that do not print are dropped) and up to 200
characters (QUESTION_MAX, shared with the desk). A blank or non-text
question, or a longer one, is refused with nothing spent. A desk loaded
before the box sends the book's question as option, which is still
taken as the question.

WEBSOCKET.md, FAQ.md and DESIGN.md describe the box and the field.

Checked: test_ws_character.py (the question test flipped to free text,
with cleaning, the limit and the old option key), test_creation.py (the
desk's examples and limit agree with the server), test_surface.py; and
in Chromium at 390x844, 820x1180 and 1366x768: an example fills the box,
a typed question with a tab and double space is sent, the log reads it
on one line, the box empties and Intuition is spent.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ETKqHLvkfH9k99JTnJzzKA
